.\" Man page for fcitx5-ainput
.TH ainput 1 "2026-10-17" "0.2.0" "fcitx5-ainput"
.SH NAME
fcitx5\-ainput \- voice input addon for fcitx5
.SH SYNOPSIS
fcitx5 addon, loaded automatically. No standalone binary.
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBfcitx5\-ainput\fP is a push-to-talk voice input addon for the fcitx5
input method framework. It captures audio via PulseAudio, performs
speech recognition through configurable ASR backends, and commits the
recognized text to the active application.

Hold \fBCapsLock\fP to start recording, release to stop and transcribe.
The recognized text is committed at the cursor position.
.PP
The input panel shows \fBlistening\fP, \fBprocessing audio\fP, and
\fBrecognizing\fP status. Network, service, timeout, microphone, and
no-speech failures are shown in that panel and are never inserted into the
application document.
.SH USAGE
.TP
\fBCapsLock\fP (long-press, default 300ms)
Start voice recording. Release to stop and transcribe.
.PP
Recording can start while an earlier cloud request is still recognizing.
Ainput preserves recording and commit order and targets the input context that
was active at the start of each recording. At most three recognitions,
including the active one, are queued. A newer recording is discarded with an
input-panel error when that limit is reached.
.TP
\fBCtrl+CapsLock\fP
Enter provider/denoiser switching mode. The notification shows the
provider's display name with the currently configured model (for example
\fBQwen · qwen-audio-3.1-asr-flash\fP, \fBDoubao · bigmodel\fP, or
\fBZipformer · <model-dir-basename> (local)\fP), read from the provider's config
file. While holding CapsLock:
.br
\fB\(<- / h\fP  \-\- previous ASR provider
.br
\fB\(-> / l\fP  \-\- next ASR provider
.br
\fB\(ua / k\fP   \-\- previous denoiser
.br
\fB\(da / j\fP   \-\- next denoiser
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration is split in two.

Shared settings (backend selection, CapsLock hold time, notification
timeout, denoiser, loudness target, suppression level and speech gate) are
stored in fcitx5's own configuration,
\fB~/.config/fcitx5/conf/ainput.conf\fP, and are editable in
\fBfcitx5-configtool\fP under Addons -> Ainput.

Per-provider data (API keys, model identifiers, endpoints, local model and
binary paths, timeouts) is stored in \fB~/.config/ainput/*.json\fP.
Each file is created on first run with every field present, its default
value and comments; files are optional and support // line comments.
Provider files are re-read before every recognition, so edits apply to the
next recording without restarting fcitx5.
Every file is validated on read: JSON syntax errors (with byte offset) are
logged and the file's values are not trusted; unknown fields get a "did you
mean" suggestion and type mismatches are named in the fcitx5 log, with the
first provider-file issue repeated as a warning line in the switch
notification.
.SS Shared (fcitx5-configtool)
The following options are stored by fcitx5 itself; the file only lists values
that differ from their default.
.TP
\fBProvider\fP (default \fBqwen\fP)
Active backend: qwen, doubao, zipformer, fire_red or mock.
\fBCtrl+CapsLock\fP switching rewrites it.
.TP
\fBActivationMsec\fP (default \fB300\fP)
How long CapsLock must be held before recording starts.
.TP
\fBNotificationTimeout\fP (default \fB2000\fP)
How long switch notifications stay visible, in milliseconds.
.TP
\fBBufferMs\fP (default \fB100\fP)
PulseAudio fragment size in milliseconds (20-1000). Raise it when the end of
a phrase is cut off on a device that delivers audio in bursts; lower it for
quicker response. There is no auto-detection.
.TP
\fBDenoise\fP (default \fBnone\fP)
none, speexdsp or deepfilter. deepfilter needs a helper binary at
~/.local/share/ainput/bin/deep-filter.
.TP
\fBLufsTarget\fP (default \fB-16\fP)
Loudness normalization target in LUFS.
.TP
\fBSpeexLevel\fP (default \fB-15\fP)
speexdsp suppression strength in dB.
.TP
\fBCrestThreshold\fP (default \fB2.4\fP)
Speech gate; lower is more permissive, 0 disables it.
.PP
Four further options accept credentials and model ids so a fresh install can
be configured entirely here: \fBQwenApiKey\fP, \fBQwenModel\fP,
\fBDoubaoApiKey\fP and \fBDoubaoModel\fP. An empty value means "not set
here"; the provider then uses \fB~/.config/ainput/<provider>.json\fP and
finally its built-in default, so an empty field never clears a key that is
already configured in the file.
.SS User-facing (must edit)
.TP
\fBdoubao.json\fP
API credentials for ByteDance Volcengine ASR plus model and timeout tuning.
Submit and result polling share one deadline, \fBtimeout_sec\fP (default 90).
.RS
.nf
{"api_key": "xxx", "resource_id": "volc.seedasr.auc"}
.fi
.RE
.TP
\fBqwen.json\fP
API key, ASR model, and recognition options for Alibaba DashScope
(Qwen-Audio ASR). The model defaults to
\fBqwen-audio-3.1-asr-flash\fP and is configurable via the \fBmodel\fP key.
.RS
.nf
{"api_key": "sk-xxx"}
.fi
.RE
.TP
\fBqwen.json\fP optional keys include \fBmodel\fP, \fBlanguage_hints\fP,
\fBvocabulary\fP, \fBvocabulary_id\fP, \fBkeep_dialect\fP,
\fBspeaker_diarization\fP and \fBtimeout_sec\fP; see
/usr/share/doc/fcitx5-ainput/config/ for commented examples.
.SS Optional (all defaults in code)
.TP
\fBzipformer.json\fP
Local Zipformer tuning: \fBmodel_dir\fP, \fBbin_path\fP, \fBtimeout_sec\fP.
.TP
\fBfire_red.json\fP
Local FireRed tuning: \fBmodel_dir\fP, \fBbin_path\fP, \fBtimeout_sec\fP.
.SH ASR PROVIDERS
.TP
\fBMock\fP
Returns "hello world" immediately. For testing without network.
.TP
\fBZipformer\fP (sherpa-onnx)
Local streaming model (about 490 MB download). Requires the
\fBsherpa-onnx\fP binary and the model file set named in the README.
.TP
\fBFireRed\fP (sherpa-onnx-offline)
Local offline AED model (about 800 MB download). Requires the
\fBsherpa-onnx-offline\fP binary.
.TP
\fBDoubao\fP (ByteDance Volcengine)
Cloud API. Requires \fBdoubao.json\fP with API key and resource ID.
.TP
\fBQwen\fP (Alibaba DashScope)
Cloud API. Requires \fBqwen.json\fP with API key.
.SH AUDIO PIPELINE
Recorded audio goes through:
.RS
.nf
PulseAudio capture
  \(-> ebur128 loudness normalization (-16 LUFS)
  \(-> denoising (speexdsp or deepfilter; only when enabled)
  \(-> VAD-based silence trimming
  \(-> WAV output
  \(-> ASR recognition
.fi
.RE
.PP
PulseAudio capture is asynchronous. On CapsLock release, Ainput returns
control to fcitx5 immediately, retains a short audio tail, then starts
processing and recognition.
.SH RELIABILITY
Doubao and Qwen use persistent serialized workers, allowing curl connections
to be reused while preserving result order. Zipformer and FireRed intentionally
run one local process per utterance.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/fcitx5/conf/ainput.conf
Shared settings, written by fcitx5.
.TP
.I ~/.config/ainput/
Per-provider configuration directory.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/ainput/pa_buffer.json
Auto-detected PulseAudio buffer sizes, keyed by source id (state, not
configuration; created automatically).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/ainput/
Optional local ASR binaries (
.IR sherpa-onnx/bin/ )
and models (
.IR models/ );
the exact layout is described in the project README.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/ainput/diagnostic.log
Developer diagnostic log; only written by builds configured with
\fB-Ddiagnostic_logging=true\fP.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/fcitx5-ainput/config/
Commented configuration examples shipped by the package.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/fcitx5/ainput.so
Addon shared library.
.TP
.I /usr/share/fcitx5/addon/ainput.conf
Addon manifest.
.SH BUGS
Report issues at https://github.com/xander-lin/ainput/issues.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fcitx5 (1)
